Chapter-1 What Is The Shell 

- Shell is a program that takes keyboard commands and passes them to the operating system to carry them out 
- All linux distributions provide a shell program from the GNU project called the bash
- We usually interact with the shell using a terminal emulator 
- Prompt Format - username@machinename (vboxuser@Ubuntu-26)_current working directory_$
- # instead of a $ indicates superuser privileges. Which means that either we are logged in as the root user or the selected terminal emulator provides admin privileges 
- Up arrow shows the last 1,000 command's history 
- ctrl+shift+v for copy and similar for pasting. Ctrl+c used to kill processes
- date - current date & time 
- cal - calendar of the month 
- df - current amount of free space on disk drives 
- free - displays the amount of free memory 
- exit - To terminate a terminal session 

